  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance for the final phase-out of methyl bromide in the post harvest sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical assistance for the final phase-out of methyl bromide in the post harvest sector. The project seeks to phase-out the remaining consumption of methyl bromide for controlled uses in Sudan. Methyl bromide is presently still used for disinfestation and quality maintenance of sorghum, held in concrete silo bins equipped with MB gas re-circulation systems. The alternative chosen for implementation and sustainable use is phosphine fumigation applied by the means of specialized infrastructure, which ensures appropriate gas re-circulation and uniform distribution, known as Closed Loop Fumigation (CLF). Phosphine fumigation takes longer to achieve disinfestation than methyl bromide, but equivalent treatment efficacy is achieved.</narrative>
  </description>
